   ],
   "rot": -160,
   "text": "THE BASILICA OF LAST LIGHT\n\nHere the kingdom kept its loudest silence.\n\nWhen the sun stood still at vespers, the choir sang the hours anyway, so the light would have somewhere to stand. Listen: the stone still holds the note."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    2.4,
    0,
    -22.6
   ],
   "rot": 140,
   "text": "THE UNRUNG BELL\n\nCast for the thirteenth hour and never swung.\n\nThe Bellkeeper would not ring it, and the Precentress would not let it rust in peace. It hangs between their two stubbornnesses, full to the lip with one unstruck note."
  },
  {
   "at": [
    -12.5,
    0,
    1.2
   ],
   "rot": 90,
   "text": "THE WEST GALLERY\n\nThe choir walked above the congregation, so their singing would fall like weather.\n\n(The stair is on the eastern side. What the choir left behind is still up there.)"
  },
  {
   "at": [
    11.2,
    0,
    -12.8
   ],
   "rot": -110,
   "text": "THE SEXTON'S BAY\n\nSix hundred brothers, one shovel.\n\nHe buried the choir one by one as the wax took them, and awaits no thanks. Graves before glory; tailings before talk."
  }
 ],
